extend ../layout.pug

block content
  h2= t('emails.transactionReactionReceived.title')
  .text-block
    include ../includes/salutation.pug
    //- The one piece of news (W1, the first wave back): who was glad of the thank-you -- and
    //- how they showed it, in a paragraph of its own and large, so that the reaction is what
    //- the eye lands on (Bernd, 27.10.2026: at the end of the sentence it went unnoticed, and
    //- the mail read like a second receipt of the transfer). The emoji stands here and nowhere
    //- else -- never in the subject, which mail clients garble with an emoji in it. The subject
    //- and the heading are the same words for every such mail; the sentence carries the name.
    //- Its size as an inline style, not a rule in the shared stylesheet: that one stands in the
    //- head of every mail the server sends.
    p= t('emails.transactionReactionReceived.hasEnjoyedYourThanks', { recipientAlias, recipientCommunity })
    p.reaction-emoji(style="font-size: 48px; line-height: 56px; margin: 8px 0 0 0;")= emoji
  .content
    //- Which thank-you is meant, named as the giver's own: the amount and, where there is one,
    //- the memo -- and no value in another currency beside it. No "transaction details", and
    //- no line that says what the two buttons below say (Bernd, 27.10.2026).
    //- The alias stays whole: as a block that moves to the next line as one piece where the
    //- heading does not fit ("Dein Dank an" / "Sarah-B" on a phone), and breaks inside only
    //- where it is wider than the card by itself. The phrase is split at its placeholder, so
    //- a language that puts the alias first (Turkish) gets the same.
    - const [beforeAlias, afterAlias] = t('emails.transactionReactionReceived.yourThanksTo', { recipientAlias: '\u0000' }).split('\u0000')
    h2
      = beforeAlias
      span.alias(style="display: inline-block; max-width: 100%; overflow-wrap: anywhere;")= recipientAlias
      = afterAlias
    div(class="p_content")= t('emails.general.amountGDD', { amountGDD: transactionAmount })
      if transactionMemo
        br
        +humanText(t('emails.transactionReactionReceived.memo', { transactionMemo }))

    //- The way to the person who reacted: their conversation, where the transfer stands.
        Green and inside the card, as every button that leads to a person (webflow.css),
        above the gold way into the account -- as the mail about an accepted link has it. The
        contact page opens the window with the member `with` names, of the community
        `community` names. Without the two uuids there is no such way, and the button is left
        out. Each of the two is written as ONE value of the address (encodeURIComponent).
    if recipientCommunityUuid && recipientUuid
      div
        a.button-5(href=`${communityURL}/contacts?with=${encodeURIComponent(recipientUuid)}&community=${encodeURIComponent(recipientCommunityUuid)}` style="margin: 25px 0 0 0")
          include ../includes/chatbox-icon.pug
          span #{t('emails.general.toConversation')}

    a.button-3(href=`${communityURL}/transactions`) #{t('emails.general.toAccount')}

    include ../includes/doNotReply.pug
